|~ `::kind` and what is declared under it: the kind, its constructor, the
   words that build it from the noun, their refusals and their laws. The
   kind of kinds and its words are written as their literals, since none of
   them stands while the source runs; the chain builds every other kind.
   The decisions it exists for: [QSBLD#kind]. ~|

:kind
  |~~ A kind: the payload its tag is laid over, the fields it reads of the
      payload, the refusals it pages and the facts they carry, the
      invariants its values hold, its laws, and for a kind of the core the
      check its host hands. It is built from the noun by commands, each a
      verb the kind so far is the subject of:
      `::kind | wraps |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map | reads :w |~~ The width. ~~| /w ::number`.
      `wraps` names the payload, its page and its kinds; `reads` a field,
      its name, its page, the place of the payload it reads, `/w` the key
      `w` and `~(query /h 1)` the key `h` or one, and its kinds; `tells` a
      page of the kind on a name, a chapter of a topic among them; `holds` an
      invariant of the value or of a field, its refusal, its page and its
      condition; `throws` a refusal and its page; `carries` a fact a
      refusal carries, its page and its kinds; `proves` a law, its page and
      its query; and `impl ::builtin{}` the check of a kind of the core. A
      value put under a kind holds the value of the kinds of its payload,
      each field read and held, and the invariants of the value, each
      refusal named under the kind, `::Box/w/KindNotTakenError`: the
      constructor attaches the tag to the payload or refuses it, and
      builds no other value. A kind declared under a
      name is a label, its words functions named under it: the payload,
      each field, each refusal, fact, invariant and law lie under it for
      `doc`, and `manifest` lists them but the laws, which `laws` reads;
      a label declared by its page alone holds its page and lays its tag
      as a kind of no commands does. It prints as its literal, its commands in a
      quote and the check of the host or null after it, and reads back
      from it.
      ::link~(::fn | doc) ::link~(::tag | doc)
      ::link~(::qlang/verbs | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind[~(wraps
        |~~ The literal of a kind: the quote of its commands and the check
            a host hands a kind of the core, `::builtin{}`, or null.
        ~~|
    | throws :PayloadNotPairError
        |~~ The literal of a kind is a pair, the commands that declare it
            and the check of the host or null:
            `::kind[~(wraps |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map) null]`.
        ~~|
    | throws :SignatureNotCommandsError
        |~~ The commands of a kind are a quote of the commands that build
            it, each with its objects: `wraps` a page and kinds, `reads` a
            name, a page, a place and kinds, `holds` a name, a page and a
            condition, `throws` a name and a page, `carries` a name, a
            page and kinds, `tells` a name and a page, and `proves` a
            name, a page and a query. The name of a field and of a page is
            one segment, beside `payload`, `construct` and the words of a
            literal; the name of a refusal, a fact and a law is read as a
            tag; a page is a doc, a place a path or a quote, and kinds a
            tag, a set of tags, or a vector of one of them for the kinds of
            each element.
        ~~|
    | throws :NameDeclaredTwiceError
        |~~ A name of a kind is declared once: the payload, each field,
            refusal, fact, invariant and law by its name, and an invariant
            names no refusal the kinds of its field name,
            `:w/KindNotTakenError`.
        ~~|
    | throws :NameUnderNoFieldError
        |~~ A refusal or an invariant written with a path is named under a
            field read before it, `:w/NegativeError`.
        ~~|
    | throws :LawUnderNoNameError
        |~~ A law written with a path is named under a name the kind
            declares before it: a field, a refusal, an invariant, a fact,
            the payload, or a refusal the kinds of the payload or of a
            field name, `proves :w/KindNotTakenError/refusesAString …`.
        ~~|
    | throws :FactUnderNoNameError
        |~~ A fact written with a path is named under a name the kind
            declares before it, the refusal that carries it,
            `carries :TooWideError/w …`.
        ~~|
    | throws :RecipeNotBuiltinError
        |~~ The second of the pair is the check a host hands a kind of the
            core, `::builtin{}`, or null: a kind attaches its tag by its
            commands, and a recipe that would build another value from the
            payload has no place in it.
        ~~|
    | proves :isBuiltByCommands
        |~~ A kind is built from the noun. ~~|
        ~(::kind | wraps |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map | type | eq ::kind)
    | proves :printsAsItsLiteral
        |~~ A kind prints as its commands and its recipe. ~~|
        ~(::kind | wraps |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map | print | eq "::kind[~(wraps |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map) null]")
    | proves :listsItsNamesButItsLaws
        |~~ `manifest` lists what lies under a kind but its laws, which
            `laws` reads.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A box. ~~| (::kind | reads :w |~~ The width. ~~| /w ::number | proves :holds |~~ It holds. ~~| ~(true))
          | ::Box
          | get [~(manifest) ~(laws | keys)]
          | eq [#[::Box/w] #[:holds]])
    | proves :laysTheTagOfALabelOfItsPageAlone
        |~~ A label declared by its page alone lays its tag. ~~|
        ~(:Shop |~~ A shop. ~~| | ::Shop{:a 1} | type | eq ::Shop)
    | proves :readsBackFromItsPrint
        |~~ The print of a kind reads back as the kind. ~~|
        ~(::kind | wraps |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map | :k it | print | parse | apply it | eq k)
    | proves :laysItsTagOverThePayload
        |~~ A value put under a kind is the payload under its tag. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | wraps |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map)
          | ::Box{:w 1}
          | get [~(type) /w]
          | eq [::Box 1])
    | proves :isALabel
        |~~ A kind declared under a name is a label the scope reads. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | wraps |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map) | kinds | has ::Box)
    | proves :refusesAPayloadOfNoneOfItsKinds
        |~~ A payload of none of the kinds `wraps` names is refused under
            the kind.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | wraps |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map) | ::Box#5 !| type | eq ::Box/PayloadKindNotTakenError)
    | proves :refusesAnElementOfNoneOfItsKinds
        |~~ Where `wraps` names the kinds of each element, an element of
            none is refused with its index.
        ~~|
        ~(:Nums |~~ Numbers. ~~| (::kind | wraps |~~ The numbers. ~~| [::number])
          | ::Nums[1 "a"]
          !| get [~(type) /index]
          |  eq [::Nums/ElementKindNotTakenError 1])
    | proves :holdsThePayloadOfItsKind
        |~~ The payload is the value of its kind beneath the tags it is
            given under.
        ~~|
        ~(:Count |~~ A count. ~~| (::kind | wraps |~~ The number. ~~| ::number) | ::Count::Width#3 | payload | eq 3)
    | proves :readsAField
        |~~ A field of none of its kinds is refused under the field. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | reads :w |~~ The width. ~~| /w ::number)
          | ::Box{:w "x"}
          !| type
          |  eq ::Box/w/KindNotTakenError)
    | proves :refusesAFieldLeftOut
        |~~ A field whose path the payload leaves out is refused. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | reads :w |~~ The width. ~~| /w ::number) | ::Box{} !| type | eq ::Box/w/NotGivenError)
    | proves :givesAFieldADefault
        |~~ A field read by `query` gives a default. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | reads :h |~~ The height. ~~| ~(query /h 1) ::number) | ::Box{} | type | eq ::Box)
    | proves :pagesAFieldUnderIt
        |~~ The page of a field is the page of its node under the kind. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | reads :w |~~ The width. ~~| /w ::number)
          | ::Box/w
          | doc
          | content
          | trim
          | eq "The width.")
    | proves :pagesTheRefusalOfTheKindsOfAField
        |~~ The refusal the kinds of a field name is paged by them where
            `throws` gives it no page.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | reads :w |~~ The width. ~~| /w ::number)
          | ::Box/w/KindNotTakenError
          | doc
          | content
          | trim
          | eq "`w` holds a value of `::number`.")
    | proves :readsNoFieldAsAWord
        |~~ A field is no word of the values of its kind: `get` reads its
            place.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | reads :w |~~ The width. ~~| ~(get /w) ::number)
          | ::Box{:w 1}
          | get [~(w !| type) /w]
          | eq [::call/UnknownNameError 1])
    | proves :holdsTheInvariantsOfItsValue
        |~~ A value that breaks an invariant of the kind is refused under
            it.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | holds :TooWideError |~~ No wider than high. ~~| ~(subOf /h /w | gte 0))
          | ::Box{:w 3 :h 2}
          !| type
          |  eq ::Box/TooWideError)
    | proves :holdsTheInvariantsOfAField
        |~~ A field that breaks an invariant written under it is refused
            under the field.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | reads :w |~~ The width. ~~| /w ::number | holds :w/NegativeError |~~ No width below zero. ~~| ~(gte 0))
          | ::Box{:w -1}
          !| type
          |  eq ::Box/w/NegativeError)
    | proves :PayloadNotPairError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no pair. ~~|
        ~(::kind[1] !| type | eq ::kind/PayloadNotPairError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesAStepThatIsNoCommand
        |~~ A step of a recipe is no command of a kind. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(add 1) null] !| type | eq ::kind/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesACommandOfAFunction
        |~~ A command of a function is no command of a kind. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0) null] !| type | eq ::kind/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesAFieldNamedWithAPath
        |~~ The name of a field is one segment. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(reads :w/x |~~ A w. ~~| /w) null] !| type | eq ::kind/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesThePayloadAsAField
        |~~ The payload is no field. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(reads :payload |~~ A payload. ~~| /p) null] !| type | eq ::kind/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesTheConstructorAsAField
        |~~ The constructor is no field. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(reads :construct |~~ A constructor. ~~| /c) null] !| type | eq ::kind/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesAPlaceThatIsNoPathOrQuote
        |~~ A place is a path or a quote. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(reads :w |~~ A w. ~~| 0) null] !| type | eq ::kind/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesASignatureThatIsNoQuote
        |~~ The commands are a quote. ~~|
        ~(::kind[[] null] !| type | eq ::kind/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :NameDeclaredTwiceError/refusesTwoFieldsOfOneName
        |~~ Two fields of one name are refused. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(reads :w |~~ A w. ~~| /w | reads :w |~~ Again. ~~| /x) null] !| type | eq ::kind/NameDeclaredTwiceError)
    | proves :NameDeclaredTwiceError/refusesAnInvariantNamedAsTheRefusalOfKinds
        |~~ An invariant named as the refusal of its field's kinds is
            refused.
        ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(reads :w |~~ A w. ~~| /w ::number | holds :w/KindNotTakenError |~~ Positive. ~~| ~(gt 0)) null] !| type | eq ::kind/NameDeclaredTwiceError)
    | proves :NameUnderNoFieldError/refusesARefusalUnderNoField
        |~~ A refusal under a name no field reads is refused. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(throws :x/TooBigError |~~ Too big. ~~|) null] !| type | eq ::kind/NameUnderNoFieldError)
    | proves :LawUnderNoNameError/refusesALawUnderNoName
        |~~ A law under a name the kind does not declare is refused. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(proves :x/holds |~~ An x. ~~| ~(true)) null] !| type | eq ::kind/LawUnderNoNameError)
    | proves :FactUnderNoNameError/refusesAFactUnderNoName
        |~~ A fact under a name the kind does not declare is refused. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~(carries :x/y |~~ A y. ~~|) null] !| type | eq ::kind/FactUnderNoNameError)
    | proves :RecipeNotBuiltinError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no check of a host. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~() 5] !| type | eq ::kind/RecipeNotBuiltinError)
    | proves :RecipeNotBuiltinError/refusesARecipe
        |~~ A recipe that would build another value is refused. ~~|
        ~(::kind[~() ~(add 1)] !| type | eq ::kind/RecipeNotBuiltinError))
    ::builtin{}]

:kind/wraps
  |~~ Names the payload of a kind, its page and its kinds,
      `::kind | wraps |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map`: a payload of none of them
      is refused under the kind, and one they reach beneath its tags is
      held as the value of its kind; a vector of kinds names the kinds of
      each element, and a payload that is no vector is refused.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on |~~ The noun itself, which starts the kind, or a kind. ~~| ::tag
    | takes :page |~~ The page of the payload. ~~| /0 ::doc
    | takes :kinds
        |~~ The kinds of the payload, a tag or a set of tags, or a vector
            of one of them for the kinds of each element; any value where
            none is given.
        ~~|
        ~(query /1 null) #[::null ::set ::tag ::vec]
    | returns |~~ The kind with its payload. ~~| ::kind
    | throws :SubjectNotKindError
        |~~ `wraps` names the payload of the noun's kind,
            `::kind | wraps …`, or of a kind.
        ~~|
    | proves :pagesThePayload
        |~~ The page of the payload is the page of its node under the
            kind.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | wraps |~~ The sizes. ~~| ::map)
          | ::Box/payload
          | doc
          | content
          | trim
          | eq "The sizes.")
    | proves :SubjectNotKindError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | wraps |~~ A number. ~~| !| type | eq ::kind/wraps/SubjectNotKindError))
    ::builtin{}]

:kind/reads
  |~~ Adds a field to a kind: its name, its page, the place of the payload
      it reads, and the kinds it holds where they are given,
      `::kind | reads :w |~~ The width. ~~| /w ::number`. The place is a
      path into the payload, `/w` the key `w`, a place the payload leaves
      out refused under the field, or a quote that reads it,
      `~(query /h 1)` the key `h` or one; a value of none of the kinds is
      refused under the field. A field is no word: `get` reads its place.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on |~~ The noun itself, which starts the kind, or a kind. ~~| ::tag
    | takes :name
        |~~ The name of the field, its node under the kind. ~~|
        /0 ::keyword
    | takes :page |~~ The page of the field. ~~| /1 ::doc
    | takes :place
        |~~ The place of the payload the field reads, a path or a quote. ~~|
        /2 #[::path ::quote]
    | throws :place/KindNotTakenError
        |~~ The place is a path, `/w`, or a quote that reads the payload,
            `~(query /h 1)`.
        ~~|
    | takes :kinds
        |~~ The kinds the field holds, a tag or a set of tags, or a vector
            of one of them for the kinds of each element; any value where
            none is given.
        ~~|
        ~(query /3 null) #[::null ::set ::tag ::vec]
    | returns |~~ The kind with the field after the ones it read. ~~| ::kind
    | throws :SubjectNotKindError
        |~~ `reads` builds from the noun, `::kind | reads …`, or a kind. ~~|
    | proves :holdsTheKindsOfEachElement
        |~~ A field of the kinds of each element refuses an element of
            none with its index.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | reads :xs |~~ Values. ~~| /xs [::number])
          | ::Box{:xs [1 "a"]}
          !| get [~(type) /index]
          |  eq [::Box/xs/ElementKindNotTakenError 1])
    | proves :readsAPathAtDepth
        |~~ A path reads a field at depth. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | reads :w |~~ The width. ~~| /size/w ::number)
          | ::Box{:size {:w "x"}}
          !| type
          |  eq ::Box/w/KindNotTakenError)
    | proves :SubjectNotKindError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | reads :w |~~ A w. ~~| /w !| type | eq ::kind/reads/SubjectNotKindError))
    ::builtin{}]

:kind/tells
  |~~ Tells a page of a kind on a name, and the kinds it tells of where
      they are given, `::kind | tells :values |~~ Values. … ~~| #[::tag ::vec]`:
      a chapter of a topic, or a page a kind keeps beside its refusals,
      laid under the kind for `doc` and `manifest`, and a law written
      under its name lies under it.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on |~~ The noun itself, which starts the kind, or a kind. ~~| ::tag
    | takes :name |~~ The name of the page. ~~| /0 ::keyword
    | takes :page |~~ The page told. ~~| /1 ::doc
    | takes :kinds
        |~~ The kinds the page tells of, a tag or a set of tags; none
            where none is given.
        ~~|
        ~(query /2 null) #[::null ::set ::tag]
    | returns |~~ The kind with the page. ~~| ::kind
    | throws :SubjectNotKindError
        |~~ `tells` writes a page of the noun's kind, `::kind | tells …`,
            or of a kind.
        ~~|
    | proves :laysThePageUnderTheKind
        |~~ A page told lies under the kind, the kinds it tells of its
            value.
        ~~|
        ~(:Guide |~~ A guide. ~~| (::kind | tells :start |~~ Where to start. ~~| #[::vec])
          | get [~(::Guide/start | doc | content | trim) ~(::Guide/start | binding | get /value)]
          | eq ["Where to start." #[::vec]])
    | proves :holdsTheLawsUnderItsName
        |~~ A law written under the name of a page lies under it. ~~|
        ~(:Guide |~~ A guide. ~~| (::kind | tells :start |~~ Where to start. ~~| | proves :start/holds |~~ It holds. ~~| ~(true))
          | ::Guide/start
          | runLaws
          | map /ok
          | eq [true])
    | proves :SubjectNotKindError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | tells :x |~~ An x. ~~| !| type | eq ::kind/tells/SubjectNotKindError))
    ::builtin{}]

:kind/carries
  |~~ Names a fact a refusal of a kind carries, its page and its kinds,
      `::kind | carries :TooWideError/w |~~ The width refused. ~~| ::number`,
      under the refusal its path names; a fact written with no path is a
      fact of the payload, as the kind of errors names the facts every
      error may carry.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on |~~ The noun itself, which starts the kind, or a kind. ~~| ::tag
    | takes :name |~~ The name of the fact. ~~| /0 ::keyword
    | takes :page |~~ The page of the fact. ~~| /1 ::doc
    | takes :kinds
        |~~ The kinds of the fact, a tag or a set of tags; any value where
            none is given.
        ~~|
        ~(query /2 null) #[::null ::set ::tag]
    | returns |~~ The kind with the fact. ~~| ::kind
    | throws :SubjectNotKindError
        |~~ `carries` names a fact of the noun's kind,
            `::kind | carries …`, or of a kind.
        ~~|
    | proves :pagesTheFactUnderItsRefusal
        |~~ A fact lies under the refusal that carries it. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | throws :TooWideError |~~ Too wide. ~~| | carries :TooWideError/w |~~ The width refused. ~~| ::number)
          | ::Box/TooWideError/w
          | doc
          | content
          | trim
          | eq "The width refused.")
    | proves :SubjectNotKindError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | kind/carries :x |~~ An x. ~~| !| type | eq ::kind/carries/SubjectNotKindError))
    ::builtin{}]

:kind/holds
  |~~ Writes an invariant of a kind: the refusal of a value that breaks it,
      its page, and the condition the payload beneath the tag answers true
      to, `| holds :TooWideError |~~ No wider than high. ~~| ~(subOf /h /w | gte 0)`;
      written with a path it holds of a field, `:w/NegativeError`, the
      value the payload gives the field.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on |~~ The noun itself, which starts the kind, or a kind. ~~| ::tag
    | takes :name
        |~~ The name of the refusal of a value that breaks it. ~~|
        /0 ::keyword
    | takes :page |~~ The page of the refusal. ~~| /1 ::doc
    | takes :condition
        |~~ The condition the value answers true to. ~~|
        /2 ::quote
    | returns |~~ The kind with the invariant. ~~| ::kind
    | throws :SubjectNotKindError
        |~~ `holds` writes an invariant of the noun's kind,
            `::kind | holds …`, or of a kind.
        ~~|
    | proves :passesAValueThatKeepsIt
        |~~ A value that keeps every invariant goes under the kind. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | holds :TooWideError |~~ No wider than high. ~~| ~(subOf /h /w | gte 0))
          | ::Box{:w 1 :h 2}
          | type
          | eq ::Box)
    | proves :SubjectNotKindError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | kind/holds :E |~~ An e. ~~| ~(true) !| type | eq ::kind/holds/SubjectNotKindError))
    ::builtin{}]

:kind/throws
  |~~ Names a refusal of a kind and its page,
      `::kind | throws :TooWideError |~~ A parcel past its height. ~~|`,
      under a field where it is written with a path, the page of the
      refusal the kinds of a field name among them; a refusal a primitive
      of the kind raises is paged so.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on |~~ The noun itself, which starts the kind, or a kind. ~~| ::tag
    | takes :name |~~ The name of the refusal. ~~| /0 ::keyword
    | takes :page |~~ The page of the refusal. ~~| /1 ::doc
    | returns |~~ The kind with the refusal. ~~| ::kind
    | throws :SubjectNotKindError
        |~~ `throws` names a refusal of the noun's kind,
            `::kind | throws …`, or of a kind.
        ~~|
    | proves :pagesTheRefusalOfKinds
        |~~ A refusal the kinds of a field name takes the page `throws`
            gives it.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | reads :w |~~ The width. ~~| /w ::number | throws :w/KindNotTakenError |~~ The width is a number. ~~|)
          | ::Box/w/KindNotTakenError
          | doc
          | content
          | trim
          | eq "The width is a number.")
    | proves :SubjectNotKindError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | kind/throws :E |~~ An e. ~~| !| type | eq ::kind/throws/SubjectNotKindError))
    ::builtin{}]

:kind/proves
  |~~ Writes a law of a kind, the claim its name makes, its page and the
      query that proves it, `| proves :holdsItsSizes |~~ … ~~| ~(…)`, which
      `laws` and `runLaws` read under the kind; a name written with a path
      lays it under a name the kind declares before it.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on |~~ The noun itself, which starts the kind, or a kind. ~~| ::tag
    | takes :name |~~ The name of the law. ~~| /0 ::keyword
    | takes :page |~~ The page of the law, the claim it proves. ~~| /1 ::doc
    | takes :query
        |~~ The query that proves the claim, answering `true`. ~~|
        /2 ::quote
    | returns |~~ The kind with the law. ~~| ::kind
    | throws :SubjectNotKindError
        |~~ `proves` writes a law of the noun's kind, `::kind | proves …`,
            or of a kind.
        ~~|
    | proves :declaresALawOfTheKind
        |~~ A law of a kind runs under it. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | proves :holds |~~ It holds. ~~| ~(true))
          | ::Box
          | runLaws
          | map /ok
          | eq [true])
    | proves :SubjectNotKindError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | kind/proves :x |~~ An x. ~~| ~(true) !| type | eq ::kind/proves/SubjectNotKindError))
    ::builtin{}]

:kind/impl
  |~~ Gives a kind of the core the check its host hands,
      `| impl ::builtin{}`, its constructor, which lies under it as
      `construct` and attaches the tag to a payload or refuses it; any
      other kind attaches its tag by its commands, and a recipe that would
      build another value from the payload is refused.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on |~~ The noun itself, which starts the kind, or a kind. ~~| ::tag
    | takes :recipe
        |~~ The check, a primitive of the host. ~~|
        /0 ::builtin
    | throws :recipe/KindNotTakenError
        |~~ The check of a kind is the host's, `::builtin{}`: a kind of
            yours attaches its tag by `wraps`, `reads` and `holds`, and a
            recipe that would build another value has no place in it.
        ~~|
    | returns |~~ The kind with its check. ~~| ::kind
    | throws :SubjectNotKindError
        |~~ `impl` gives the check of the noun's kind, `::kind | impl …`,
            or of a kind.
        ~~|
    | proves :liesUnderTheKindAsItsConstructor
        |~~ The check lies under the kind as its constructor. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A parcel. ~~| (::kind | impl ::builtin{}) | ::Box/construct | binding | get /value | eq ::builtin{})
    | proves :recipe/KindNotTakenError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no check. ~~|
        ~(::kind | impl 5 !| type | eq ::kind/impl/recipe/KindNotTakenError)
    | proves :recipe/KindNotTakenError/refusesAQuote
        |~~ A recipe that would build another value is refused. ~~|
        ~(::kind | impl ~(add 1) !| type | eq ::kind/impl/recipe/KindNotTakenError)
    | proves :SubjectNotKindError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | kind/impl ::builtin{} !| type | eq ::kind/impl/SubjectNotKindError))
    ::builtin{}]
